This is for drawing **two cards without replacement** from a standard 52-card deck. The numerator counts the 6 possible ace pairs, and the denominator counts all 1,326 possible two-card hands.

You mentioned the formula:

\[
P(\text{two aces})=\frac{C(4,2)}{C(52,2)}
=\frac{6}{1326}
=\frac{1}{221}
\approx 0.00452.
\]

Here, \(C(4,2)\) counts ways to choose two of the four aces, and \(C(52,2)\) counts all possible two-card draws from the 52-card deck, without replacement.
